{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RJky4V1zwS4wNaKhPLUdA7","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on the context filesystem, I found the information about the cluster mirroring design RPC method renames:\\\\n\\\\n## Final Names for Cluster Mirroring RPC Methods\\\\n\\\\nAccording to KIP-1279 (Cluster Mirroring) design discussions, the RPC methods were **renamed** as follows:\\\\n\\\\n- **AddTopicsToMirror** → **StartMirrorTopics**\\\\n- **RemoveTopicsFromMirror** → **StopMirrorTopics**\\\\n\\\\nThis refinement was made during the extended community review phase in response to Andrew Schofield's detailed review comments (noted as AS27 in the discussion).\\\\n\\\\n### Sources:\\\\n- **kips-and-discussions.md** (line 218): \\\\\\\"**Mirror State Operations (AS27)**: Refined semantics: AddTopicsToMirror/RemoveTopicsFromMirror → StartMirrorTopics/StopMirrorTopics\\\\\\\"\\\\n- **window-96-summary.md** (lines 220): \\\\\\\"Mirror state management: Refined AddTopicsToMirror/RemoveTopicsFromMirror to StartMirrorTopics/StopMirrorTopics\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nThe change was part of the broader KIP-1279 design refinement addressing security/authorization models, topic ID usage, producer ID transformation, and failover/failback workflows in cluster mirroring.\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"store\\\",\\\"kips-and-discussions.md\\\",\\\"window-96-summary.md\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":17.85,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":1,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":76735,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":10385,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.0354915,\\\"input_tokens\\\":58,\\\"output_tokens\\\":1398}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"893809fe-8dce-44df-a24c-8dc0a2ff6938","uuid":"51ac874c-0198-4207-b4de-e3ce54d46693","timestamp":"2026-09-27T19:06:49.736Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on the context filesystem, I found the information about the cluster mirroring design RPC method renames:\\\\n\\\\n## Final Names for Cluster Mirroring RPC Methods\\\\n\\\\nAccording to KIP-1279 (Cluster Mirroring) design discussions, the RPC methods were **renamed** as follows:\\\\n\\\\n- **AddTopicsToMirror** → **StartMirrorTopics**\\\\n- **RemoveTopicsFromMirror** → **StopMirrorTopics**\\\\n\\\\nThis refinement was made during the extended community review phase in response to Andrew Schofield's detailed review comments (noted as AS27 in the discussion).\\\\n\\\\n### Sources:\\\\n- **kips-and-discussions.md** (line 218): \\\\\\\"**Mirror State Operations (AS27)**: Refined semantics: AddTopicsToMirror/RemoveTopicsFromMirror → StartMirrorTopics/StopMirrorTopics\\\\\\\"\\\\n- **window-96-summary.md** (lines 220): \\\\\\\"Mirror state management: Refined AddTopicsToMirror/RemoveTopicsFromMirror to StartMirrorTopics/StopMirrorTopics\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nThe change was part of the broader KIP-1279 design refinement addressing security/authorization models, topic ID usage, producer ID transformation, and failover/failback workflows in cluster mirroring.\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"store\\\",\\\"kips-and-discussions.md\\\",\\\"window-96-summary.md\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":17.85,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":1,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":76735,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":10385,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.0354915,\\\"input_tokens\\\":58,\\\"output_tokens\\\":1398}}\"}","_meta":{"fastmcp":{"wrap_result":true}},"structuredContent":{"result":"{\"answer\":\"Based on the context filesystem, I found the information about the cluster mirroring design RPC method renames:\\n\\n## Final Names for Cluster Mirroring RPC Methods\\n\\nAccording to KIP-1279 (Cluster Mirroring) design discussions, the RPC methods were **renamed** as follows:\\n\\n- **AddTopicsToMirror** → **StartMirrorTopics**\\n- **RemoveTopicsFromMirror** → **StopMirrorTopics**\\n\\nThis refinement was made during the extended community review phase in response to Andrew Schofield's detaile